  triage:title "SHUTDOWN_FINALIZER_THREADS static Mutex lacks inline rationale comment (RBP-006)" ;
  triage:description "runtime_health.rs:40: static SHUTDOWN_FINALIZER_THREADS: std::sync::Mutex<Vec<std::thread::JoinHandle<()>>> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Vec::new()); — no inline comment explaining why a static Mutex is the correct model vs. a thread-local or per-test struct. Add a brief comment: static registry is necessary because run_bounded_shutdown_step is a static fn with no instance reference; test cleanup drains handles via drain_shutdown_finalizer_threads_for_test." ;
